# Tracer: proof methods with a complete goal and no user-written proof body
#
# Before (did not work):
# by extension {1} = {1}
# by enumerate finite_set forall x {1, 2} => {x = 1 or x = 2}
# by for forall i1 range(0, 3) => {i1 < 3}
# Former behavior: each line was rejected because its goal appeared on the by-header.
#
# Now (verified):
by extension {1} = {1}
by enumerate finite_set forall x {1, 2} => {x = 1 or x = 2}
by for forall i1 range(0, 3) => {i1 < 3}
# Current behavior: each line constructs the existing proof statement with an empty user proof.
#
# Boundary: an inline goal cannot also own an indented proof body; use the existing
# `by extension:`, `by enumerate finite_set:`, or `by for:` goal-block form instead.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/01_proof_patterns/inline_by_proof_methods.lit
